From a45b46c98f969aae52b1250fe13c02054f9f9c01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 10:17:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: Try slurp when the request includes monitors

The default chooser list skipped slurp unless the request was for
monitors only. When the compositor supports toplevel capture, clients
such as OBS request MONITOR | WINDOW, so slurp was never spawned and
the portal fell through to the dmenu-style choosers.

Run slurp whenever monitors are among the requested types. slurp can
only select outputs, so window sharing through the default chooser
requires slurp to be absent or a dmenu-type chooser_cmd to be set.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
---
 src/screencast/chooser.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/screencast/chooser.c b/src/screencast/chooser.c
index 7d66898..947eba1 100644
--- a/src/screencast/chooser.c
+++ b/src/screencast/chooser.c
@@ -234,7 +234,7 @@ static bool wlr_chooser_default(struct xdpw_screencast_context *ctx, struct xdpw
 	bool ret;
 	for (size_t i = 0; i<N; i++) {
 		const struct xdpw_chooser *chooser = &default_chooser[i];
-		if (chooser->type == XDPW_CHOOSER_SIMPLE && type_mask != MONITOR) {
+		if (chooser->type == XDPW_CHOOSER_SIMPLE && !(type_mask & MONITOR)) {
 			continue;
 		}
 		ret = wlr_chooser(chooser, ctx, target, type_mask);
-- 
